    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green. The repository's test suite consists of the `AcceptanceTest` (the project's single acceptance suite), which passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (which generates `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `membershipNumber` using an expression that calls a null-safe `membershipNumber(Owner)` helper, following the existing `displayName`/`initials` pattern. It computes `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, returning `null` when either `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent (e.g. legacy seed owners), matching how those nullable fields already behave.\n\nSince the value is derived from the owner's own persisted fields (`customerCode`, `registrationDate`), it appears consistently on both the POST-create response and GET responses without needing a separate `Assign` step or entity column.",
